<title>GERMANY: Hochtief - 96 charges strengthen finances.</title>
<headline>Hochtief - 96 charges strengthen finances.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Hochtief AG said on Tuesday it wrote off 323 million marks related to its shareholdings in rival Phillip Holzmann AG and other units.</p>
<p>Since Holzmann shares have risen since the end of the year, the early write-off has left Hochtief with increased financial reserves, chief executive Hans-Peter Keitel told a news conference.</p>
<p>Hochtief, which reported 1996 net profit of 146.1 million marks, owns 24.9 percent of Holzmann shares directly and holds a contract to buy another 10 percent held by Commerzbank AG.</p>
<p>Hochteif also took charges of 130 million marks related the the elimination of 2,300 jobs in Germany, Keitel said.</p>
<p>-- Neal Boudette, Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
